---
layout: base.njk
title: What clients say
description: A few words from people Sarah has coached.
---
{#- Screen 2b. As on 2a, title and description are the design's own h1 and lead,
    used verbatim rather than written fresh.

    No contactFooter here: its absence is what gives this page the compact dark
    footer the design draws, rather than the homepage's full contact block.

    No permalink either — Eleventy maps this file to /testimonials/, which is
    what the nav and the homepage teaser already link to, and what makes
    aria-current="page" fire in header.njk. -#}

{#- TODO-SARAH: the testimonials themselves. All three are the design's
    placeholder, which announces itself on the page. Sarah's real words replace
    the two strings per entry and nothing else.

    A list plus a loop rather than three copy-pasted blocks, the same call
    header.njk made for the nav: the markup is identical every time and only the
    strings differ. The briefing asks for two to five of these, so the count
    lives in one visible place and is one line to change. The grey/periwinkle
    banding is not here — it is a nth-child rule in pages.css, so adding or
    removing an entry cannot get the sequence wrong.

    The em dash sits in the template below and only the name and role are data,
    so a replacement is a paste of Sarah's text with no punctuation to match. -#}
{% set testimonials = [
  { quote: "Placeholder testimonial — three to four lines of client copy from Sarah goes here, fixed-size block.", by: "Client name, role" },
  { quote: "Placeholder testimonial — three to four lines of client copy from Sarah goes here, fixed-size block.", by: "Client name, role" },
  { quote: "Placeholder testimonial — three to four lines of client copy from Sarah goes here, fixed-size block.", by: "Client name, role" }
] %}

<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-head__title">What clients say</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lead">A few words from people Sarah has coached.</p>
</div>

<section class="testimonials">
  {%- for t in testimonials %}

  {#- A blockquote where the design has a plain div, and a footer where it has a
      second span — these are quotations with an attribution, the same call
      index.njk made for the homepage teaser. No <cite>: that element is for the
      title of a work, not a person's name.

      aria-hidden on the quote glyph. It is ornament, and without this a screen
      reader announces a stray quote mark before every testimonial. -#}
  <blockquote class="testimonial">
    <span class="testimonial__mark" aria-hidden="true">"</span>
    <p class="testimonial__quote">{{ t.quote }}</p>
    <footer class="testimonial__by">— {{ t.by }}</footer>
  </blockquote>
  {%- endfor %}

  {#- The design's button points at screen 2d, so this is the Book page and not
      the homepage's Calendly marker. Must stay the last child: the banding rule
      in pages.css counts children, and a card after this one would be
      miscoloured. -#}
  <a class="button" href="/book/">Book a consultation</a>
</section>
